/**
 * Cloudflare Workers Static Assets config for the Astro Starlight
 * documentation site at packages/docs-site-astro/.
 *
 * **Phase 1-5 status: PREVIEW ONLY.** The production
 * `annot.work/docs/*` route still belongs to the legacy VitePress
 * worker (`packages/docs-site/wrangler.jsonc`). This config
 * deploys to a preview origin so we can smoke-test the Astro
 * build without touching production. The route is added in
 * Phase 6 (`docs/plans/annot-work-astro-unification.md`).
 *
 * Phase 6 cutover plan: feature-flag based — both workers run
 * in parallel, a header / cookie picks which serves a given
 * request. The Phase 6 PR adds the route + the picker Worker.
 *
 * URL layout once cutover lands:
 *
 *   annot.work/      → annot-marketing (landing)
 *   annot.work/app/* → annot (PWA at /app/)
 *   annot.work/docs/*→ THIS worker (Astro Starlight)
 *   annot.work/api/* → annot-api
 *
 * Astro is configured with `base: "/docs/"` so every internal
 * link in the built HTML already includes that prefix.
 * `not_found_handling: "404-page"` because Astro emits a
 * per-route static file — falling through to an index page
 * would be wrong.
 *
 * The preview origin (`docs-astro-preview.annot.work` or a
 * `workers.dev` subdomain — provisioned by the maintainer)
 * still needs `workers_dev: false` flipped to `true` OR a
 * routes pattern targeting the preview hostname; this is left
 * for the maintainer to wire up alongside the Cloudflare
 * account setup. The on-disk build artefact in `./dist/docs/`
 * is correct either way; only the `routes` / `workers_dev`
 * lines differ between preview + production.
 */
{
  "name": "annot-docs-site-astro",
  "compatibility_date": "2026-04-23",
  "main": "./worker.js",
  // Preview-only flag for Phase 1-5. Phase 6 PR flips this and
  // adds the production route block to claim annot.work/docs/*.
  "workers_dev": true,
  "preview_urls": true,
  "assets": {
    "directory": "./dist",
    "binding": "ASSETS",
    "not_found_handling": "404-page"
  }
}
